{"authored" [{"question" "q-338254" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $D(y)=xy\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+3y,$ then $D(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/state.json" "file_sha256" "55fbafc9e2e48fe0073f53c838fa7ce1d9b5ce450a7006828fa01dd6f56d408e" "basis" 1279 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-338254" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{3}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+{f}_{2}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x,y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x,y)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{3}=xy,{f}_{2}=0,{f}_{1}=0,$ and ${f}_{0}=3.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x) & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\cdot (-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x(3-8x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/state.json" "file_sha256" "55fbafc9e2e48fe0073f53c838fa7ce1d9b5ce450a7006828fa01dd6f56d408e" "basis" 1279 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-338254" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6477498f472159f5747d570aac6faa791ca10b4dbb98a45ae4f566f3ce2a9d48" "basis" 1279 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-338254" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/state.json" "file_sha256" "55fbafc9e2e48fe0073f53c838fa7ce1d9b5ce450a7006828fa01dd6f56d408e" "basis" 1279 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-338254" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/state.json" "file_sha256" "55fbafc9e2e48fe0073f53c838fa7ce1d9b5ce450a7006828fa01dd6f56d408e" "basis" 1279 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-338254" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x(3+8x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/state.json" "file_sha256" "55fbafc9e2e48fe0073f53c838fa7ce1d9b5ce450a7006828fa01dd6f56d408e" "basis" 1279 "verification" "/home/jak