/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/state.json" "file_sha256" "55fbafc9e2e48fe0073f53c838fa7ce1d9b5ce450a7006828fa01dd6f56d408e" "basis" 1279 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $D=\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}}{\\textrm d x^{2}}+3 \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}+5,$ what is $D(y)$ for $y=e^{- x}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/example-6570.json" "file_sha256" "3ed4a497316367d92234ca742519c942ed787c800f7349ac831e3e0aeab33c6d" "basis" 1279 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y) = a_{2}\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}y}{\\textrm d x^{2}} + a_{1}\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm d x} + a_0y\n$$\n\nwith constant coefficients  $a_2 = 1, a_1 = 3,$ and $a_0 = 5.$ \n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D({e}^{-x}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}+5){e}^{-x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}({e}^{-x})+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{-x})+5{e}^{-x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{e}^{-x})+3\\cdot (-{e}^{-x})+5{e}^{-x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}-3{e}^{-x}+5{e}^{-x} \\\\  & =3{e}^{-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/example-6570.json" "file_sha256" "3ed4a497316367d92234ca742519c942ed787c800f7349ac831e3e0aeab33c6d" "basis" 1279 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6571" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $D=x^2\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}}{\\textrm d x^{3}}-5x \\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}}{\\textrm d x^{2}} +9\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x},$ what is $D(y)$ for $y=\\ln{x}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/example-6571.json" "file_sha256" "ce645281fc9c60208fab5c7c2507dee82c450a8ec5648d1fc53a2d9b1f9637f7" "basis" 1279 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6571" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y) = f_{3}(x)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}y}{\\textrm d x^{3}} + f_{2}(x)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}y}{\\textrm d x^{2}} + f_{1}(x)\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm d x} + f_0(x)y.\n$$\n\nwith $f_3 = x^2, f_2 = -5x, f_1 = 9,$ and $f_0 = 0.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & =({x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}-5x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+9\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x})\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-5x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+9\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\frac{1}{x})-5x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{x})+9\\cdot (\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})-5x(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})+\\frac{9}{x} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}})+\\frac{5}{x}+\\frac{9}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{5}{x}+\\frac{9}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/example-6571.json" "file_sha256" "ce645281fc9c60208fab5c7c2507dee82c450a8ec5648d1fc53a2d9b1f9637f7" "basis" 1279 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-21785" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $D(y)=y\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}y}{\\textrm d x^{3}} - \\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x} + y^3,$ then calculate $D(e^{3x}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/example-21785.json" "file_sha256" "d33dca2d94e1edeaa154ba10eefe5b9e787725047388a70d2767f41dcec52604" "basis" 1279 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-21785" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y) = f_{3}(x,y)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}y}{\\textrm d x^{3}} +  f_{2}(x,y)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}y}{\\textrm d x^{2}} + f_{1}(x,y)\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm d x} + f_0(x,y)y\n$$\n\nwith $f_3 = y,  f_2 = 0,  f_1 = -1,$ and $f_0 = y^2.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y = e^{3x}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D({e}^{x}) & ={e}^{3x}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}({e}^{3x})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{3x})+{({e}^{3x})}^{3} \\\\  & ={e}^{3x}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(3{e}^{3x})-3\\cdot {e}^{3x}+{e}^{9x} \\\\  & ={e}^{3x}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(9{e}^{3x})-3\\cdot {e}^{3x}+{e}^{9x} \\\\  & =27{e}^{6x}-3\\cdot {e}^{3x}+{e}^{9x} \\\\  & ={e}^{3x}({e}^{6x}+27{e}^{3x}-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/example-21785.json" "file_sha256" "d33dca2d94e1edeaa154ba10eefe5b9e787725047388a70d2767f41dcec52604" "basis" 1279 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036386/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-337833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $D=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}+1,$ what is $D(y)$ for $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-337833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={a}_{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{a}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{a}_{0}y\n$$\n\nwith constant coefficients  ${a}_{2}=1,{a}_{1}=5,$ and ${a}_{0}=1.$ \n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)) \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))+5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))+1\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))+5\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-337833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0848faaf54cde4afb10b4dd127b1b307ee9977bf2e5fceb231dff9d47dae5545"} {"question" "q-337833" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-337833" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)"] ["math" "5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-337833" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-91033" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $D=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x},$ what is $D(y)$ for $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-91033" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={a}_{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{a}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{a}_{0}y\n$$\n\nwith constant coefficients  ${a}_{2}=1,{a}_{1}=-2,$ and ${a}_{0}=0.$ \n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x})(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-2(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-91033" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0848faaf54cde4afb10b4dd127b1b307ee9977bf2e5fceb231dff9d47dae5545"} {"question" "q-91033" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-91033" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] ["math" "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] ["math" "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-91033" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-130252" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $D=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x},$ what is $D(y)$ for $y={sin}^{2}⁡x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-130252" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={a}_{3}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+{a}_{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{a}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{a}_{0}y\n$$\n\nwith constant coefficients  ${a}_{3}=1,{a}_{2}=0,{a}_{1}=2,$ and ${a}_{0}=0.$ \n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x) \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}){sin}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}({sin}^{2}⁡x)+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({sin}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+2\\cdot (\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+2\\