text{d}x}-5,$ what is $D(y)$ for $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-337831" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={a}_{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{a}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{a}_{0}y\n$$\n\nwith constant coefficients  ${a}_{2}=1,{a}_{1}=2,$ and ${a}_{0}=-5.$ \n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)) \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}-5)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x))+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x))-5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))+2\\cdot (3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x) \\\\  & =-9\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x) \\\\  & =-14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-337831" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0848faaf54cde4afb10b4dd127b1b307ee9977bf2e5fceb231dff9d47dae5545"} {"question" "q-337831" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget"