{aligned}D(y) & =D(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & =(x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x})\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\  & =x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{x})+\\frac{2}{x} \\\\  & =x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})+\\frac{2}{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{2}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-65037" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0848faaf54cde4afb10b4dd127b1b307ee9977bf2e5fceb231dff9d47dae5545"} {"question" "q-65037" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-65037" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{2}{x}"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{x}"] ["math" "x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-65037" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{x}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-130082" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $D=x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x},$ what is $D(y)$ for $y={x}^{2}-2x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-130082" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}=x,{f}_{1}=1,$ and ${f}_{0}=0.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D({x}^{2}-2x) \\\\  & =(x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x})({x}^{2}-2x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}({x}^{2}-2x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}-2x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x-2)+(2x-2) \\\\  & =2x+2x-2 \\\\  & =4x-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-130082" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0848faaf54cde4afb10b4dd127b1b307ee9977bf2e5fceb231dff9d47dae5545"} {"question" "q-130082" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-130082" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "4x"] ["math" "4x-2"] ["math" "x+2"] ["math" "x+4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-130082" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4x-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-91045" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $D={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}-2x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x},$ what is $D(y)$ for $y={x}^{4}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-91045" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{3}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+{f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y.\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{3}={x}^{2},{f}_{2}=-2x,{f}_{1}=x,$ and ${f}_{0}=0.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D({x}^{4}) \\\\  & =({x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}-2x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}){x}^{4} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}({x}^{4})-2x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}({x}^{4})+x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{4}) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(4{x}^{3})-2x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{x}^{3})+x(4{x}^{3}) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(12{x}^{2})-2x(12{x}^{2})+4{x}^{4} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(24x)-24{x}^{3}+4{x}^{4} \\\\  & =24{x}^{3}-24{x}^{3}+4{x}^{4} \\\\  & =4{x}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-91045" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0848faaf54cde4afb10b4dd127b1b307ee9977bf2e5fceb231dff9d47dae5545"} {"question" "q-91045" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-91045" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "16{x}^{3}"] ["math" "48{x}^{3}"] ["math" "4{x}^{3}-24{x}^{2}"] ["math" "4{x}^{4}"] ["math" "4{x}^{4}+16{x}^{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-91045" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4{x}^{4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-337840" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $D={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}+2,$ what is $D(y)$ for $y={x}^{2}-1?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-337840" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}={x}^{2},{f}_{1}=3,$ and ${f}_{0}=2.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D({x}^{2}-1) \\\\  & =({x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}+2)({x}^{2}-1) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}({x}^{2}-1)+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}-1)+2({x}^{2}-1) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x)+3(2x)+2({x}^{2}-1) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\cdot 2+6x+2{x}^{2}-2 \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}+6x-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-337840" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0848faaf54cde4afb10b4dd127b1b307ee9977bf2e5fceb231dff9d47dae5545"} {"question" "q-337840" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/ques