2}({x}^{2}+1)+5({x}^{2}+1) \\\\  & =2({x}^{2}+1)-2{x}^{2}({x}^{2}+1)+5({x}^{2}+1) \\\\  & =7({x}^{2}+1)-2{x}^{2}({x}^{2}+1) \\\\  & =({x}^{2}+1)(7-2{x}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-337848" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0848faaf54cde4afb10b4dd127b1b307ee9977bf2e5fceb231dff9d47dae5545"} {"question" "q-337848" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-337848" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "({x}^{2}+1)(2{x}^{2}-7)"] ["math" "({x}^{2}+1)(5-2{x}^{2})"] ["math" "({x}^{2}+1)(7+2{x}^{2})"] ["math" "({x}^{2}+1)(7-2{x}^{2})"] ["math" "({x}^{2}+1)(7-{x}^{2})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-337848" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "({x}^{2}+1)(7-2{x}^{2})"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-337972" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $D(y)=y\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3{y}^{2},$ then $D({e}^{-2x})=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-337972" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{2}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x,y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x,y)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}=y,{f}_{1}=2y,$ and ${f}_{0}=3y.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y={e}^{-2x}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D({e}^{-2x}) & ={e}^{-2x}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}({e}^{-2x})+2({e}^{-2x})\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{-2x})+3{({e}^{-2x})}^{2} \\\\  & ={e}^{-2x}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2{e}^{-2x})+2{e}^{-2x}\\cdot (-2{e}^{-2x})+3{e}^{-4x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-2x}\\cdot 4{e}^{-2x}-4{e}^{-4x}+3{e}^{-4x} \\\\  & =4{e}^{-4x}-4{e}^{-4x}+3{e}^{-4x} \\\\  & =3{e}^{-4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-337972" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0848faaf54cde4afb10b4dd127b1b307ee9977bf2e5fceb231dff9d47dae5545"} {"question" "q-337972" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-337972" "field" "selecti