^{2}}(3{x}^{2})-2x({x}^{3}+1)\\cdot 3{x}^{2}+4({x}^{3}+1) \\\\  & =({x}^{3}+1)\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6x)-6{x}^{3}({x}^{3}+1)+4({x}^{3}+1) \\\\  & =({x}^{3}+1)\\cdot 6-6{x}^{3}({x}^{3}+1)+4({x}^{3}+1) \\\\  & =6({x}^{3}+1)-6{x}^{3}({x}^{3}+1)+4({x}^{3}+1) \\\\  & =10+4{x}^{3}-6{x}^{6} \\\\  & =2(5+2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{6})\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-338186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0848faaf54cde4afb10b4dd127b1b307ee9977bf2e5fceb231dff9d47dae5545"} {"question" "q-338186" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-338186" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2(-5-2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{6})"] ["math" "2(5+2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{6})"] ["math" "2(5+2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{6})"] ["math" "2(5+4{x}^{3}-3{x}^{6})"] ["math" "2(5-2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{6})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "q-338186" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2(5+2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{6})"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/state.json" "file_sha256" "fe7396a35486c8db5583b39d1bee3cf7377ecd3e0331949a4bfe951fb5c016f7"} {"question" "e-6570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $D=\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}}{\\textrm d x^{2}}+3 \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}+5,$ what is $D(y)$ for $y=e^{- x}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/example-6570.json" "file_sha256" "d7b5c493c4cb696a99e2679f1aca8eff4d9a67cea5e0d2adad9d7c5db876e3d3"} {"question" "e-6570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y) = a_{2}\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}y}{\\textrm d x^{2}} + a_{1}\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm d x} + a_0y\n$$\n\nwith constant coefficients  $a_2 = 1, a_1 = 3,$ and $a_0 = 5.$ \n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D({e}^{-x}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}+5){e}^{-x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}({e}^{-x})+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{-x})+5{e}^{-x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{e}^{-x})+3\\cdot (-{e}^{-x})+5{e}^{-x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}-3{e}^{-x}+5{e}^{-x} \\\\  & =3{e}^{-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/example-6570.json" "file_sha256" "d7b5c493c4cb696a99e2679f1aca8eff4d9a67cea5e0d2adad9d7c5db876e3d3"} {"question" "e-6571" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $D=x^2\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}}{\\textrm d x^{3}}-5x \\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}}{\\textrm d x^{2}} +9\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x},$ what is $D(y)$ for $y=\\ln{x}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/example-6571.json" "file_sha256" "cc8e3366c4a72c553e92d59c8b00a160399762648e0f0a659eb923c92a5f4d17"} {"question" "e-6571" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y) = f_{3}(x)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}y}{\\textrm d x^{3}} + f_{2}(x)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}y}{\\textrm d x^{2}} + f_{1}(x)\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm d x} + f_0(x)y.\n$$\n\nwith $f_3 = x^2, f_2 = -5x, f_1 = 9,$ and $f_0 = 0.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & =({x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}-5x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+9\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x})\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-5x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+9\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\frac{1}{x})-5x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{x})+9\\cdot (\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})-5x(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})+\\frac{9}{x} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}})+\\frac{5}{x}+\\frac{9}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{5}{x}+\\frac{9}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/example-6571.json" "file_sha256" "cc8e3366c4a72c553e92d59c8b00a160399762648e0f0a659eb923c92a5f4d17"} {"question" "e-21785" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $D(y)=y\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}y}{\\textrm d x^{3}} - \\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x} + y^3,$ then calculate $D(e^{3x}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/example-21785.json" "file_sha256" "2a42dccbed6cde059fc9c04092cf0e34b8bf5ae31e709cf6effadd5f8d351046"} {"question" "e-21785" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y) = f_{3}(x,y)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}y}{\\textrm d x^{3}} +  f_{2}(x,y)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}y}{\\textrm d x^{2}} + f_{1}(x,y)\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm d x} + f_0(x,y)y\n$$\n\nwith $f_3 = y,  f_2 = 0,  f_1 = -1,$ and $f_0 = y^2.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y = e^{3x}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D({e}^{x}) & ={e}^{3x}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}({e}^{3x})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{3x})+{({e}^{3x})}^{3} \\\\  & ={e}^{3x}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(3{e}^{3x})-3\\cdot {e}^{3x}+{e}^{9x} \\\\  & ={e}^{3x}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(9{e}^{3x})-3\\cdot {e}^{3x}+{e}^{9x} \\\\  & =27{e}^{6x}-3\\cdot {e}^{3x}+{e}^{9x} \\\\  & ={e}^{3x}({e}^{6x}+27{e}^{3x}-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072215/example-21785.json" "file_sha256" "2a42dccbed6cde059fc9c04092cf0e34b8bf5ae31e709cf6effadd5f8d351046"}] "usage" {"e-21785" [] "q-338254" [] "q-65037" [] "e-6571" [] "e-6570" []} "basis" 2625 "retractions" [[17592186079080 :question/problem "Given that $D = x\\frac{d^{2}}{dx^{2}} + 2\\frac{d}{dx}$, what is $D(y)$ for $y = \\ln x$?"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186077692 17592186077693 17592186077694 17592186077695 17592186077696 17592186297574 17592186297575 17592186297576 17592186297577 17592186297578] "immutable_fields" [[17592186077691 :answer-field/correct] [17592186077691 :answer-field/id] [17592186077691 :answer-field/key] [17592186077691 :answer-field/type] [17592186297573 :answer-field/correct] [17592186297573 :answer-field/id] [17592186297573 :answer-field/key] [17592186297573 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
